Z||000000||rnoswal||10-10-2000||11:43 PM||||I read from the archives that someone had found seats from f-body GM products that bolt right into the Fiero. They said seats from a 97 Firebird and 96 Camaro. Anyone with any other years and just how well they fit?<P>Russ<P>------------------<BR>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000001||msweldon||10-11-2000||09:14 AM||||Can't give you much additional details but I too have seen Grand Am leather seats as well as firebird seats in a fiero.  It does take away some head room, due to the power seating system, so if your 6'3" like I am you may not want to consider it.  I'll respond with the URL if I can find it.<P>later,<BR>marc||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||10-11-2000||11:21 AM||||Based on other threads on this topic, I believe that 82 to present F-body seats will fit. You will probably have to "slot" the holes in the rear of the brackets. I've also heard that the right side seat should use the Fiero tracks instead of the F-bod. <BR>I also have heard of people using F-bod seats in S-10s, so the S-10 seats <I>may</I> fit, as well.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||the need for speed||10-11-2000||01:32 PM||||why does the right side need to be monted on the fiero tracks?????????||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-11-2000||08:52 PM||||The F-body has a weird shape to the right side floor pan to clear the cat. converter so the seat rails are made to fit that shape instead of a flat pan like the Fiero.||||reg||1
